<p>More than 80 film workers and Berlin International Film Festival (Berlinale) alumni, including actors Javier Bardem and Tilda Swinton, have signed an open letter criticizing what they call the festival’s “silence” on Israel’s war in Gaza. Reports said the letter was sent to AFP and published on Tuesday. The dispute comes after comments by Berlinale jury president Wim Wenders, who said the jury should avoid being drawn into politics when asked about Gaza.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/GO8MlTwbBGguF587tSdZfWYUgI54oFHXirBf3URAT40uVYt-7gqfqzgzN4T6eNUugEJVy9bjl8lDtUt6Yyj3tfAT0WnpEOxGKbswhTz4q-13oggE0tKCt06jSWaBwwnBNL3M1iulJSZ-ZLTqYAyBa2VL2lvkWqub0e12fFTpk0pNpH_dYN_o9qbqoaFdWJoyob-j7A4RoPjluApw4whGQWDcFu3lEDD5dGVrQ_e_ae_NTi0u7dRupxzu6g' alt='Bae Doona (left) and Berlinale jury president Wim Wenders at a Berlinale jury press conference in Berlin, February 12, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Letter language: The signatories said they were “appalled” by what they called the Berlinale’s “institutional silence,” and “dismayed” by what they described as involvement in censoring artists who oppose Israel’s actions in Gaza.</li><li>Allegations raised: Al Jazeera reported that the letter accused the festival of “anti-Palestinian racism,” casting the dispute as not only about geopolitics but also about how Palestinian voices are treated.</li><li>Named signatories: In addition to Bardem and Swinton, the Guardian reported that filmmaker Adam McKay signed the open letter.</li><li>Industry pressure: The Straits Times noted that the entertainment industry has faced calls before to take a stance on Gaza, placing the Berlinale debate within a broader cultural conversation.</li></ul><blockquote>We cannot really enter the field of politics. - Wim Wenders</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Open-letter signatories (film workers and alumni): They urged Berlinale organizers to take a stance on Gaza, echoing broader, recurring calls for the entertainment industry to speak out on the issue. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/over-80-berlin-film-festival-alumni-sign-open-letter-urging-organisers-to-take-stance-on-gaza'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Wim Wenders (Berlinale jury president): He said the jury should not “enter the field of politics” when asked about Gaza. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2026/feb/17/javier-bardem-and-tilda-swinton-among-those-to-condemn-berlinales-silence-on-gaza'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Berlinale leadership: The festival director defended filmmakers who chose not to comment on Gaza. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/javier-bardem-tilda-swinton-among-signatories-denouncing-berlinale-s-gaza-silence/a-76012687'>DW</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/culture/article/2026/02/17/in-an-open-letter-dozens-of-film-figures-slam-berlin-film-festival-silence-on-gaza_6750590_30.html'>In an open letter, dozens of film figures slam Berlin Film Festival &#x27;silence&#x27; on Gaza</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/18/over-80-film-workers-slam-berlin-festivals-silence-on-israels-gaza-war'>Over 80 film workers slam Berlin festival’s silence on Israel’s Gaza war</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/javier-bardem-tilda-swinton-among-signatories-denouncing-berlinale-s-gaza-silence/a-76012687'>Javier Bardem, Tilda Swinton among signatories denouncing Berlinale&#x27;s Gaza &#x27;silence&#x27;</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2026/feb/17/javier-bardem-and-tilda-swinton-among-those-to-condemn-berlinales-silence-on-gaza'>Javier Bardem and Tilda Swinton among those to condemn Berlinale’s ‘silence’ on Gaza</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/over-80-berlin-film-festival-alumni-sign-open-letter-urging-organisers-to-take-stance-on-gaza'>Over 80 Berlin Film Festival alumni sign open letter urging organisers to take stance on G